{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_S2y5N7Y5u8OLgsvUHpSuo4x4","content":"1\t# xlang slice 1 findings\n2\t\n3\tCompleted on `feat/xlang-matrix` in commit `e5888d91` (`feat(yang): the cross_lang tests compose published exports; no rewriting`).\n4\t\n5\t## What the muse partial work got right\n6\t\n7\t- The ordinary-module donor composition is the correct seam: source is parsed and lowered unmodified, the donor body runs under its own `run-main`, and only runtime namespace values are projected.\n8\t- The TypeScript linked harness supplies the right content store and three vector VM runners; `yang.call`, `js`, and the published `php` module compose without pair-specific wrappers.\n9\t- The rebuilt tests pin both directions, identity, PHP opaque arrays, PHP null, and backend agreement with five assertions in three tests.\n10\t\n11\t## What was wrong and changed\n12\t\n13\t- `php/global-peek` was the wrong export path for these cases. A PHP arrow function assigned to `$phpfn` is a PersistentArrayMap Closure descriptor, not the inner function cell. TypeScript can reject that descriptor as a non-function, and logging it can fall into number rendering. `php/callable-fn` intentionally preserves an already-eligible descriptor, so it does not solve the identity requirement.\n14\t- The PHP donors now use ordinary named functions and exports use `php/resolve-fn`, exactly as the existing `source-call-test` composition does. This preserves the donor's function cell identity without call-node rewriting, foreign `:code` extraction, or a language-pair wrapper.\n15\t- Each export is explicitly bound by a UAST `let` in the caller task before projection. No cell is carried as a host value between tasks.\n16\t- Documentation now names PHP's global function table rather than `$GLOBALS` for the export source.\n17\t\n18\t## Gates\n19\t\n20\t- Parser classes were initially absent; `clojure -M:antlr-gen` restored the standard generated sources before running the focused suite.\n21\t- `clojure -M:test -n yang.cross-lang-test`: **Ran 3 tests containing 5 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.**\n22\t- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: **0 errors, 0 warnings.**\n23\t- `mise exec -- cljstyle check test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: **passed.**\n24\t\n25\tNo slice-2 Python or Clojure legs were started."}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_JrmWaDhvIP8dlWXX3f9l9pd8","content":"1\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\n2\t  \"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\n3\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\n4\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\n5\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\n6\t   task, one run.\n7\t\n8\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\n9\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\n10\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\n11\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, PHP's `phpfn` function) and projected into the caller\n12\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\n13\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\n14\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\n15\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\n16\t\n17\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\n18\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\n19\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\n20\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\"\n21\t  (:require\n22\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n23\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\n27\t  (testing \"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\"\n28\t    (is (= \"4\"\n29\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n30\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n31\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\"]))))\n32\t  (testing \"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\"\n33\t    (is (= \"yes\"\n34\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n35\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n36\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\"])))))\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\n40\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n41\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"true 5\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n42\t           (xl/call [:php \"<?php function phpfn($a, $b) { return $a + $b; }\"]\n43\t                    [\"phpfn\"]\n44\t                    [:typescript\n45\t                     \"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\"])))))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(deftest python-calls-typescript-closure-test\n49\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\"\n50\t    (is (= {:py/out [\"22\"], :py/exception nil}\n51\t           (xl/call [:typescript\n52\t                     (str \"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \"\n53\t                          \"return stored === f ? f(20) + 1 : -1; };\")]\n54\t                    [\"ts_apply\"]\n55\t                    [:python \"print(ts_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\"])))))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(deftest typescript-calls-python-closure-test\n59\t  (testing \"Python stores and calls the same TS function cell it received\"\n60\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"22\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n61\t           (xl/call [:python\n62\t                     (str \"def py_apply(f):\\n\"\n63\t                          \"    global stored\\n\"\n64\t                          \"    stored = f\\n\"\n65\t                          \"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\")]\n66\t                    [\"py_apply\"]\n67\t                    [:typescript\n68\t                     \"console.log(py_apply(x => x + 1));\"])))))\n69\t\n70\t\n71\t(deftest python-calls-php-closure-test\n72\t  (testing \"PHP stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\"\n73\t    (is (= {:py/out [\"22\"], :py/exception nil}\n74\t           (xl/call [:php\n75\t                     (str \"<?php function php_apply($f) { global $stored; \"\n76\t                          \"$stored = $f; return $stored === $f ? $f(20) + 1 : -1; }\")]\n77\t                    [\"php_apply\"]\n78\t                    [:python \"print(php_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\"])))))\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(deftest php-calls-python-closure-test\n82\t  (testing \"Python stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n83\t    (is (= \"22\"\n84\t           (xl/call [:python\n85\t                     (str \"def py_apply(f):\\n\"\n86\t                          \"    global stored\\n\"\n87\t                          \"    stored = f\\n\"\n88\t                          \"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\")]\n89\t                    [\"py_apply\"]\n90\t                    [:php \"<?php echo py_apply(function($x) { return $x + 1; });\"])))))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(deftest limits-test\n94\t  (testing \"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\"\n95\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn($a = 7) { return $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a); }\"]\n96\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\n97\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\n98\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"3n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n99\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n100\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n101\t                      [:typescript \"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\"])))))\n102\t  (testing \"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\"\n103\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn() { return null; }\"]\n104\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"false false\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n105\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n106\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n107\t                      [:typescript\n108\t                       \"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\"]))))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_7Ry2YmYzIskQiJQ9YRwydaNd","content":"1\t(ns yang.call.conformance\n2\t  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n3\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n4\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n5\t\n6\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n7\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n8\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n9\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`), reads each\n10\t   named export from the donor runtime's global namespace, and projects it\n11\t   into the caller runtime's namespace under the same name; then the caller\n12\t   source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own entry. The composition is\n13\t   a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is rewritten, no foreign\n14\t   `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is inserted, and the\n15\t   projected value is the donor's own function cell (identity survives).\n16\t\n17\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n18\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n19\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n20\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n21\t\n22\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n23\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n24\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php` is published beside them.\n25\t   The AST walker is not a backend: its links are refused until L-b.\"\n26\t  (:require\n27\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n28\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n29\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\n30\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n31\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n32\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n33\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n34\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n35\t    [yang.python.antlr.lower :as py-lower]\n36\t    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as py-parser]\n37\t    [yang.python.antlr.prelude :as py-prelude]\n38\t    [yang.python.antlr.render :as py-render]\n39\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n40\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n41\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n42\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n43\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n44\t\n45\t\n46\t(def ^:private published-php\n47\t  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n48\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n49\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n50\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n51\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n52\t\n53\t\n54\t(def ^:private published-py\n55\t  \"`py` published beside `js` and `php`, over the same host registry and\n56\t   `yang.call` revision.\"\n57\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n58\t           (py-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n59\t                                   (:call-address @h/published)))))\n60\t\n61\t\n62\t(defn- parse-ok\n63\t  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n64\t  [parse source]\n65\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\n66\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n67\t      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n68\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n69\t    pk))\n70\t\n71\t\n72\t(defn- python-export-symbol\n73\t  [export]\n74\t  (symbol (str \"xlang.python.export.\" export)))\n75\t\n76\t\n77\t(defn- python-unit\n78\t  [packet exports]\n79\t  (u/lam [py-lower/globals-sym py-lower/globals-fn-sym]\n80\t         (u/seq-nodes\n81\t           (concat (map (fn [export]\n82\t                          (u/sexp->uast\n83\t                            (list 'py/global-set py-lower/globals-sym\n84\t                                  {:py/str export} (python-export-symbol export))))\n85\t                        exports)\n86\t                   [(py-lower/lower-module-body packet)]))))\n87\t\n88\t\n89\t(def frontends\n90\t  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n91\t\n92\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n93\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n94\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n95\t   - `:unit`: packet and projected exports to the lowered unit its\n96\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\n97\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n98\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP's named-function table, Python's main\n99\t     module dictionary);\n100\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n101\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name;\n102\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n103\t  {:typescript\n104\t   {:runtime 'js,\n105\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\n106\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n107\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n108\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit packet))),\n109\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n110\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n111\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n112\t    :render render/output},\n113\t   :php\n114\t   {:runtime 'php,\n115\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\n116\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n117\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n118\t    :unit (fn [packet _] (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet))),\n119\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n120\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n121\t                   (list 'php/resolve-fn (str/lower-case export) export)),\n122\t    :project (fn [name value]\n123\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n124\t    :render php-h/render},\n125\t   :python\n126\t   {:runtime 'py,\n127\t    :address #(:address @published-py),\n128\t    :refusal [:yang.python.antlr/refusal :yang.python.antlr/undeclared-free],\n129\t    :parse #(parse-ok py-parser/parse-source %),\n130\t    :unit python-unit,\n131\t    :run-main 'py/run-main,\n132\t    :read-export (fn [export]\n133\t                   (list 'py/global-get\n134\t                         (list 'py/module-dict\n135\t                               (list 'py/modules-ref {:py/str \"__main__\"}))\n136\t                         {:py/str export})),\n137\t    :project (fn [name value]\n138\t               (list 'yin/def (list 'quote (python-export-symbol name)) value)),\n139\t    :render py-render/output}})\n140\t\n141\t\n142\t(defn- profile\n143\t  [frontend]\n144\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\n145\t      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n146\t\n147\t\n148\t(defn publish-donor!\n149\t  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n150\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n151\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n152\t  ([frontend source]\n153\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n154\t  ([frontend source module]\n155\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit]} (profile frontend)\n156\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n157\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\n158\t                refusal-key reason (h/registry)\n159\t                {:name module,\n160\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\n161\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n162\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source) []))]),\n163\t                 :exports '#{body},\n164\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\n165\t                 :runtime-address (address)})\n166\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n167\t     {:frontend frontend,\n168\t      :module module,\n169\t      :address (:address result),\n170\t      :links (:links result)})))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t(defn- runtime-entry\n174\t  \"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\"\n175\t  [frontend-keys]\n176\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\n177\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\n178\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n179\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \"init!\")))]))\n180\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\n181\t\n182\t\n183\t(defn- donor-run\n184\t  \"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\"\n185\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\n186\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\n187\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\n188\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \"body\")))])\n189\t\n190\t\n191\t(defn export-program\n192\t  \"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\n193\t   global namespace after its body ran.\"\n194\t  [donor export]\n195\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\n196\t    (u/mark-tails\n197\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\n198\t                           (donor-run donor)\n199\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\n200\t\n201\t\n202\t(defn compose\n203\t  \"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\n204\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\n205\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\n206\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\"\n207\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n208\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\n209\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\n210\t    (u/mark-tails\n211\t      (u/seq-nodes\n212\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\n213\t                (donor-run donor)\n214\t                (map (fn [export]\n215\t                       (let [value (symbol (str \"xlang.export.\" export))]\n216\t                         (u/let1 value\n217\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (read-export export))\n218\t                                 (u/sexp->uast (project export value)))))\n219\t                     exports)\n220\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source) exports))])))))\n221\t\n222\t\n223\t(defn link-source\n224\t  \"The serving composition naming the runtimes and the donor module.\"\n225\t  [{:keys [module address]}]\n226\t  (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\n227\t             'js (:address @h/published),\n228\t             'php (:address @published-php),\n229\t             'py (:address @published-py),\n230\t             module address}))\n231\t\n232\t\n233\t(defn- modules\n234\t  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it.\"\n235\t  []\n236\t  (php-prelude/admit (h/registry)))\n237\t\n238\t\n239\t(defn run-program\n240\t  \"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\"\n241\t  [donor ast]\n242\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\n243\t    (into (sorted-map)\n244\t          (map (fn [backend]\n245\t                 [backend\n246\t                  (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:modules (modules),\n247\t                                                       :link-source src}))]))\n248\t          (keys h/backends))))\n249\t\n250\t\n251\t(defn agreed\n252\t  \"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\n253\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\"\n254\t  [results]\n255\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\n256\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\n257\t\n258\t\n259\t(defn call\n260\t  \"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\n261\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\n262\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\n263\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\"\n264\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n265\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)\n266\t        render (:render (profile caller-frontend))]\n267\t    (agreed (update-vals (run-program donor (compose donor exports caller-frontend\n268\t                                                     caller-source))\n269\t                         render))))"}
