{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_78enEiMdhuiHvBhG5DIMAA3l","content":"1\t(ns yang.clojure\n2\t  \"Yang Clojure compiler - Compiles Clojure code into Yin VM Universal AST.\n3\t\n4\t  This is the Clojure-specific compiler in the Yang compiler collection.\n5\t  It transforms Clojure s-expressions into the Universal AST format that\n6\t  the Yin VM can execute. It handles:\n7\t  - Literals (numbers, strings, booleans, nil, collections)\n8\t  - Variables (symbols)\n9\t  - Lambda expressions (fn)\n10\t  - Function application (including stream operations via module system)\n11\t  - Conditionals (if)\n12\t  - Let bindings (let)\n13\t  - Top-level definitions via explicit yin/def store effects\n14\t  - Macro definitions (defmacro)\n15\t\n16\t  Macro support (docs/design/yin.vm.macro.md §10.2):\n17\t  - defmacro is a special form that lowers to ordinary (yin/def name (fn ...))\n18\t    syntax. The lambda node carries `:macro? true`, a frontend-internal fact\n19\t    the encoder (`yin.vm.encoder/program-batch`) turns into a declaration row;\n20\t    the canonical lambda row has no macro slot.\n21\t  - A macro call is an ordinary application. The frontend does no macro\n22\t    lookup: the row-native expander recognizes the call.\n23\t  - compile-program threads a compile-time macro-env naming the defmacros\n24\t    seen so far, only so the native defn lowering yields to a user defn macro.\n25\t\n26\t  Stream operations (stream/make, stream/put, stream/take, >!, <!) are compiled\n27\t  as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.\n28\t\n29\t  The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js.\"\n30\t  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\n31\t  (:require [yang.core.call :as call]\n32\t            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n33\t\n34\t\n35\t;; Forward declaration for mutual recursion\n36\t(declare compile-form compile-lambda)\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(defn literal?\n40\t  \"Check if a value is a literal (self-evaluating).\"\n41\t  [form]\n42\t  (or (number? form)\n43\t      (string? form)\n44\t      (true? form)\n45\t      (false? form)\n46\t      (nil? form)\n47\t      (keyword? form)\n48\t      (vector? form)\n49\t      (set? form)\n50\t      (map? form)))\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(defn constant-form?\n54\t  \"True when compiling `form` yields a fixed value independent of the\n55\t   environment: scalars, quoted forms, and collections built entirely from\n56\t   constants. A symbol is never constant (it is a variable reference). A\n57\t   `quote` counts as constant only at the top level: nested inside a\n58\t   collection it must reach compile-form so the quote is stripped and the\n59\t   inner form evaluated as data.\"\n60\t  ([form] (constant-form? form true))\n61\t  ([form top-level?]\n62\t   (cond\n63\t     (or (nil? form) (number? form) (string? form)\n64\t         (true? form) (false? form) (keyword? form)) true\n65\t     (and (seq? form) (empty? form)) true\n66\t     (seq? form) (and top-level? (= 2 (count form)) (= 'quote (first form)))\n67\t     (or (vector? form) (set? form)) (every? #(constant-form? % false) form)\n68\t     (map? form) (and (every? #(constant-form? % false) (keys form))\n69\t                      (every? #(constant-form? % false) (vals form)))\n70\t     :else false)))\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t(defn- compile-constructed-collection\n74\t  \"Lower a collection literal with dynamic elements to constructor calls over\n75\t   existing portable primitives, so unquoted vectors/maps/sets evaluate their\n76\t   elements like Clojure. Constant collections stay :literal nodes.\n77\t\n78\t   [e1 e2 ...]  => (conj [] e1 e2 ...)\n79\t   #{e1 e2 ...} => (conj #{} e1 e2 ...)\n80\t   {k1 v1 ...}  => (assoc {} k1 v1 k2 v2 ...)\"\n81\t  [form tail? env macro-env]\n82\t  (let [ctor (cond\n83\t               (vector? form) ['conj []]\n84\t               (set? form) ['conj #{}]\n85\t               :else ['assoc {}])\n86\t        [op seed] ctor\n87\t        args (if (map? form)\n88\t               (into [] (interleave (keys form) (vals form)))\n89\t               (vec form))\n90\t        call {:type :application,\n91\t              :operator {:type :variable, :name op},\n92\t              :operands (into [{:type :literal, :value seed}]\n93\t                              (map #(compile-form % false env macro-env) args))}]\n94\t    (cond-> call tail? (assoc :tail? true))))\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t(def initial-macro-env\n98\t  \"Compile-time map of macro names known before any defmacro: none. The\n99\t   standard forms live in the expander's store, not here.\"\n100\t  {})\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t(defn- shadow-macro-env\n104\t  \"Remove shadowed names from the macro environment.\"\n105\t  [macro-env names]\n106\t  (apply dissoc macro-env names))\n107\t\n108\t\n109\t(defn- strip-symbol-meta\n110\t  \"Return an equal symbol without reader metadata.\"\n111\t  [sym]\n112\t  (if (namespace sym)\n113\t    (symbol (namespace sym) (name sym))\n114\t    (symbol (name sym))))\n115\t\n116\t\n117\t(defn- body-expression\n118\t  [body-forms]\n119\t  (cond\n120\t    (empty? body-forms) nil\n121\t    (= 1 (count body-forms)) (first body-forms)\n122\t    :else (cons 'do body-forms)))\n123\t\n124\t\n125\t(defn- mentions-recur?\n126\t  \"True when `form` holds a recur that could target the enclosing function:\n127\t   quoted data and nested fn/loop/def forms own their own recurs.\"\n128\t  [form]\n129\t  (cond\n130\t    (seq? form) (let [head (first form)]\n131\t                  (cond\n132\t                    (= 'recur head) true\n133\t                    (contains? #{'quote 'fn 'loop 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro} head) false\n134\t                    :else (boolean (some mentions-recur? form))))\n135\t    (coll? form) (boolean (some mentions-recur? form))\n136\t    :else false))\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t;; =============================================================================\n140\t;; Sequential destructuring (slice 3)\n141\t;; =============================================================================\n142\t;;\n143\t;; A destructuring pattern lowers to ordinary symbol bindings over one\n144\t;; evaluated temporary, walked with the VM's total primitives first/rest/\n145\t;; empty? (the data module's `nth` is vector-only and refuses a list, but\n146\t;; LaTTe terms are lists):\n147\t;;\n148\t;;   [a b & r :as w] against t\n149\t;;   =>  a (first t)    c1 (rest t)\n150\t;;       b (first c1)   c2 (rest c1)\n151\t;;       r (if (empty? c2) nil c2)                        ; nthnext\n152\t;;       w t\n153\t;;\n154\t;; A nil input, a missing element and an exhausted `&` tail all yield nil,\n155\t;; as in Clojure. A non-nil remainder is a vector, the VM `rest` contract.\n156\t;; Those primitives are bare names a local binding could shadow, so a\n157\t;; destructuring form is rejected wherever first, rest or empty? is bound\n158\t;; locally. Under the convention, a guest rest definition uses raw data\n159\t;; cursors instead; previously stored definitions are not detectable here.\n160\t;; Generated names carry the reserved `dsg__` prefix and derive from the\n161\t;; binding's position, so lowering is deterministic.\n162\t\n163\t(def ^:private helper-names\n164\t  (set (map symbol [\"first\" \"rest\" \"empty?\"])))\n165\t\n166\t\n167\t(defn- locals\n168\t  [env]\n169\t  (::locals env #{}))\n170\t\n171\t\n172\t(defn- with-locals\n173\t  [env names]\n174\t  (when-let [hit (and (::convention env) (some #{'conj 'vec} names))]\n175\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"Binding \" hit \" would capture the argument-vector constructor\")\n176\t                    {:names names})))\n177\t  (when (and (::invoker env) (some #{'invoke-value} names))\n178\t    (throw (ex-info \"Binding invoke-value would capture the guest collection invoker\" {:names names})))\n179\t  (assoc env ::locals (into (locals env) (remove #(= '& %)) names)))\n180\t\n181\t\n182\t(def ^:private reserved-prefix \"dsg__\")\n183\t\n184\t\n185\t(defn- reject!\n186\t  [message data]\n187\t  (throw (ex-info message data)))\n188\t\n189\t\n190\t(defn- reserved-name?\n191\t  [sym]\n192\t  (= reserved-prefix (subs (name sym) 0 (min (count (name sym))\n193\t                                             (count reserved-prefix)))))\n194\t\n195\t\n196\t(defn- check-def-name!\n197\t  \"A definition name is a plain symbol outside the reserved prefix.\"\n198\t  [operator sym]\n199\t  (when-not (and (symbol? sym) (nil? (namespace sym)))\n200\t    (reject! (str operator \" needs a plain symbol name\") {:name sym}))\n201\t  (when (reserved-name? sym)\n202\t    (reject! \"Definition name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n203\t             {:name sym, :prefix reserved-prefix})))\n204\t\n205\t\n206\t(defn- check-binder!\n207\t  \"A binder is a plain symbol or a nested sequential pattern; anything else\n208\t   (maps, keywords, literals) is outside the supported surface.\"\n209\t  [b pattern]\n210\t  (cond\n211\t    (and (symbol? b) (nil? (namespace b)) (not= '& b))\n212\t    (when (reserved-name? b)\n213\t      (reject! \"Binding name uses the reserved destructuring prefix\"\n214\t               {:binder b, :prefix reserved-prefix}))\n215\t    (vector? b) nil\n216\t    (map? b) (reject! \"Map destructuring is not supported\"\n217\t                      {:binder b, :pattern pattern})\n218\t    :else (reject! \"Unsupported binding form\" {:binder b, :pattern pattern})))\n219\t\n220\t\n221\t(defn- parse-sequential-pattern\n222\t  \"Split a pattern vector into {:positional [...] :rest binder? :as sym?},\n223\t   rejecting malformed shapes.\"\n224\t  [pattern]\n225\t  (loop [xs (seq pattern), positional [], rest-binder ::none, as-sym nil]\n226\t    (if (nil? xs)\n227\t      {:positional positional, :rest rest-binder, :as as-sym}\n228\t      (let [x (first xs)]\n229\t        (cond\n230\t          (= '& x)\n231\t          (do (when (not= ::none rest-binder)\n232\t                (reject! \"Pattern has more than one &\" {:pattern pattern}))\n233\t              (when (or (nil? (next xs)) (= :as (second xs)))\n234\t                (reject! \"& needs a binder\" {:pattern pattern}))\n235\t              (check-binder! (second xs) pattern)\n236\t              (recur (nnext xs) positional (second xs) as-sym))\n237\t          (= :as x)\n238\t          (let [sym (second xs)]\n239\t            (when-not (and (symbol? sym) (nil? (namespace sym)) (not= '& sym))\n240\t              (reject! \":as needs a symbol\" {:pattern pattern}))\n241\t            (check-binder! sym pattern)\n242\t            (when (nnext xs)\n243\t              (reject! \":as must be last in a pattern\" {:pattern pattern}))\n244\t            (recur nil positional rest-binder sym))\n245\t          (keyword? x)\n246\t          (reject! \"Unsupported keyword in pattern\" {:keyword x, :pattern pattern})\n247\t          :else\n248\t          (do (when (not= ::none rest-binder)\n249\t                (reject! \"Only :as may follow the & binder\" {:pattern pattern}))\n250\t              (check-binder! x pattern)\n251\t              (recur (next xs) (conj positional x) rest-binder as-sym)))))))\n252\t\n253\t\n254\t(defn- first-form\n255\t  [cursor meta-map]\n256\t  (cond-> (list 'first cursor)\n257\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n258\t\n259\t\n260\t(defn- rest-form\n261\t  [cursor meta-map env]\n262\t  ;; Parameter and loop destructuring can be emitted after outcome lowering.\n263\t  ;; Keep their cursors raw vectors even when the guest library defines rest\n264\t  ;; with the argument-vector/outcome convention.\n265\t  (cond-> (if (contains? (::defined env) 'rest)\n266\t            (list 'data/subvec (list 'vec cursor) (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) 0 1))\n267\t            (list 'rest cursor))\n268\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n269\t\n270\t\n271\t(defn- nthnext-form\n272\t  \"Clojure's nthnext at a cursor: nil once exhausted, else the remainder.\"\n273\t  [cursor meta-map]\n274\t  (cond-> (list 'if (list 'empty? cursor) nil cursor)\n275\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n276\t\n277\t\n278\t(defn- temp-symbol\n279\t  [path meta-map]\n280\t  (cond-> (symbol (str reserved-prefix path))\n281\t    meta-map (with-meta meta-map)))\n282\t\n283\t\n284\t(defn- destructure-sequential\n285\t  \"Flat [sym form ...] bindings destructuring `pattern` against symbol `t`.\n286\t   A chain of cursors walks the value with first/rest; `path` names the\n287\t   generated temporaries so nested patterns stay distinct.\"\n288\t  [pattern t path env]\n289\t  (let [{:keys [positional rest as]} (parse-sequential-pattern pattern)\n290\t        m (meta pattern)\n291\t        n (count positional)\n292\t        cursor (fn [i] (if (zero? i) t (temp-symbol (str path \"c\" i) m)))\n293\t        bind (fn [out b form sub-path]\n294\t               (if (vector? b)\n295\t                 (let [sub (temp-symbol sub-path (meta b))]\n296\t                   (-> out (conj sub form) (into (destructure-sequential b sub sub-path env))))\n297\t                 (conj out b form)))\n298\t        out (reduce (fn [out [i b]]\n299\t                      (cond-> (bind out b (first-form (cursor i) m) (str path \"_\" i))\n300\t                        (or (< (inc i) n) (not= ::none rest))"}
