{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_pxUEyjWcv9HBShCPrxKOLThS","content":"1\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\n2\t  \"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\n3\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\n4\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\n5\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\n6\t   task, one run.\n7\t\n8\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\n9\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\n10\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\n11\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, PHP's `phpfn` function) and projected into the caller\n12\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\n13\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\n14\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\n15\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\n16\t\n17\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\n18\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\n19\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\n20\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\"\n21\t  (:require\n22\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n23\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\n27\t  (testing \"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\"\n28\t    (is (= \"4\"\n29\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n30\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n31\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\"]))))\n32\t  (testing \"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\"\n33\t    (is (= \"yes\"\n34\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n35\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n36\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\"])))))\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\n40\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n41\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"true 5\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n42\t           (xl/call [:php \"<?php function phpfn($a, $b) { return $a + $b; }\"]\n43\t                    [\"phpfn\"]\n44\t                    [:typescript\n45\t                     \"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\"])))))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(deftest python-calls-typescript-closure-test\n49\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\"\n50\t    (is (= {:py/out [\"22\"], :py/exception nil}\n51\t           (xl/call [:typescript\n52\t                     (str \"globalThis.ts_apply = f => { globalThis.stored = f; \"\n53\t                          \"return stored === f ? f(20n) + 1n : -1n; };\")]\n54\t                    [\"ts_apply\"]\n55\t                    [:python \"print(ts_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\\n\"])))))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(deftest typescript-calls-python-closure-test\n59\t  (testing \"Python stores and calls the same TS function cell it received\"\n60\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"22n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n61\t           (xl/call [:python\n62\t                     (str \"def py_apply(f):\\n\"\n63\t                          \"    global stored\\n\"\n64\t                          \"    stored = f\\n\"\n65\t                          \"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\")]\n66\t                    [\"py_apply\"]\n67\t                    [:typescript\n68\t                     \"console.log(py_apply(x => x + 1n));\"])))))\n69\t\n70\t\n71\t(deftest python-calls-php-closure-test\n72\t  (testing \"PHP stores and calls the same Python function cell it received\"\n73\t    (is (= {:py/out [\"22\"], :py/exception nil}\n74\t           (xl/call [:php\n75\t                     (str \"<?php function php_apply($f) { global $stored; \"\n76\t                          \"$stored = $f; return $stored === $f ? $f(20) + 1 : -1; }\")]\n77\t                    [\"php_apply\"]\n78\t                    [:python \"print(php_apply(lambda x: x + 1))\\n\"])))))\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(deftest php-calls-python-closure-test\n82\t  (testing \"Python stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n83\t    (is (= \"22\"\n84\t           (xl/call [:python\n85\t                     (str \"def py_apply(f):\\n\"\n86\t                          \"    global stored\\n\"\n87\t                          \"    stored = f\\n\"\n88\t                          \"    return f(20) + 1 if stored is f else -1\")]\n89\t                    [\"py_apply\"]\n90\t                    [:php \"<?php echo py_apply(function($x) { return $x + 1; });\"])))))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t;; Named skip: yang.clojure <-> TypeScript, both directions. yang.clojure has\n94\t;; convention-wired application lowering, but no published runtime module,\n95\t;; run-main entry, or runtime global namespace through which the shared helper\n96\t;; can run a donor and project exports. Adding those would be frontend work,\n97\t;; not a test-only composition through this helper. The test below pins the\n98\t;; skip: the helper refuses :clojure as not admitted, so admitting the\n99\t;; frontend turns this test red and the legs must be written for real.\n100\t\n101\t\n102\t(deftest clojure-typescript-cross-lang-skip-test\n103\t  (testing \"named skip: yang.clojure <-> TypeScript, both directions\"\n104\t    (is (thrown-with-msg? clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo #\"frontend not admitted\"\n105\t          (xl/call [:clojure \"(defn clj-apply [f] (+ (f 20) 1))\"]\n106\t                   [\"clj_apply\"]\n107\t                   [:typescript \"console.log(clj_apply);\"])))))\n108\t\n109\t\n110\t(deftest limits-test\n111\t  (testing \"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\"\n112\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn($a = 7) { return $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a); }\"]\n113\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\n114\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\n115\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"3n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n116\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n117\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n118\t                      [:typescript \"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\"])))))\n119\t  (testing \"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\"\n120\t    (let [src \"<?php function phpfn() { return null; }\"]\n121\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"false false\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n122\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n123\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n124\t                      [:typescript\n125\t                       \"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\"]))))))"}
